  "score": {
   "kind": "score",
   "asserts": "end-to-end weighted mean + z. w = linspace(10,1,m) rescaled so sum(w) == m; score = SUM mask[i]*w[L]*g[i][L] / (m * SUM mask[i]); z = (score - 0.5) / sigma_null(n_scored). Both sides float64.",
   "tol": 1e-09,
   "weights_note": "w = linspace(10, 1, 30) * 30 / 165",
   "heat_note": "`heat` and `masked` are per TOKEN, not per row, and have length n_tokens. Row i covers ids[i .. i+n-1] and its heat is attributed to the CURRENT token i+n-1. The leading ngram_len-1 tokens are in no window's current position, so they carry neutral heat 0.5 and masked=1 — they contribute nothing to the score, which is exactly what `masked` means on the wire (§9.2 TokenHeat).",
   "masked_note": "masked=1 means the row left BOTH the numerator and the denominator. mask[i] = rep_mask[i] * eos_mask[i].",
